cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use privacy-gate in research, please cite it as below."
title: "privacy-gate: a very small second gate that catches health data, credentials and personal data written as prose"
authors:
  - family-names: Bichel
    given-names: Yauhen
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/MoleCare/privacy-gate-llm"
url: "https://huggingface.co/YauhenBichel/privacy-gate-llm"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-22
keywords:
  - privacy
  - pii-detection
  - phi-detection
  - guardrails
  - llm-router
  - embeddings
abstract: >-
  A logistic head of 1,024 weights over BAAI/bge-m3 embeddings that answers one question about a text,
  "must this stay on this machine?", and may only ever add a hold behind whatever deterministic rules already
  run. On a 206-example invented gold set it reaches ROC AUC 0.9927 five-fold, catching 110 of 111 sensitive
  examples at 5.3 % friction, where a regex ruleset catches 9 %.
